{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 190,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Around nineteen-hundred, all of physics, and\nparticularly Einstein, was in trouble: they"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 5070,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "couldn't figure out how anything could move…"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 7310,
    "dDurationMs": 2829,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now before you complain that I'm exaggerating,\ncheck out this cat!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 10139,
    "dDurationMs": 4270,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You can clearly see that the cat is moving\naway from Einstein at a constant velocity…"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 14409,
    "dDurationMs": 4461,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but do a little sliding switcheroo, and suddenly\nit looks like Einstein's the one moving."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 18870,
    "dDurationMs": 2819,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is the \"old-fashioned principle of relativity,\"\nso of course it's the one we teach in schools…"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 21689,
    "dDurationMs": 4311,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but the point is that the switcheroo changes\nrelative things, like position and velocity,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 26000,
    "dDurationMs": 3930,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and not absolute ones, like the separation\nof Einstein from his cat."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 29930,
    "dDurationMs": 4559,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now for the problem: before Einstein was even\nborn, physicists showed that the speed of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 34489,
    "dDurationMs": 4961,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "light was one of those absolute things which\ncan't be changed by a switcheroo, so any switcheroo"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 39450,
    "dDurationMs": 3390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we do has to keep light moving at the same\nspeed."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 42840,
    "dDurationMs": 3489,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But then it's obvious that we can't do our\nsliding switcheroo at all, which means we"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 46329,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "can't explain how anything other than light\ncan move!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 48809,
    "dDurationMs": 2061,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Ok, I spoke too soon…"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 50870,
    "dDurationMs": 2189,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "there is one solution – do you see it?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 53059,
    "dDurationMs": 4680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We were assuming that our switcheroo had to\nkeep every slice of time at the same, well,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 57739,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 58739,
    "dDurationMs": 3490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But there's no law of physics that says time\nis an absolute thing that can't be changed"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 62229,
    "dDurationMs": 1191,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by switcheroos…"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 63420,
    "dDurationMs": 4580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so if we just rotate the slices of time while\nsliding them, then we can keep the speed of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 68000,
    "dDurationMs": 3250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "light the same, and explain how things can\nmove, too."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 71250,
    "dDurationMs": 4650,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Of course, Einstein didn't figure out this\n\"special principle of relativity\" in 1905"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 75900,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- it was already done by a guy named Lorentz\nten years earlier."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 78700,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But Lorentz just thought this time-rotation\nwas a mathematical trick… and it took Einstein"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 82780,
    "dDurationMs": 4580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to step in, and, you guessed it, propose that\n\"time-rotation\" is real, that time really"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 87360,
    "dDurationMs": 5480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is relative, and that consequently, simultaneous\nevents relative to one observer aren't simultaneous"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 92840,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "relative to another who's moving."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 94280,
    "dDurationMs": 13430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now that's a real switcheroo of perspective."
    } ]
  } ]
}
